WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
The UN Charter rests on the sovereign
equality of all its members.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Yet in 2005, UN members endorsed a
responsibility to protect populations from

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:15.770
genocide, war crimes, ethnic
cleansing and crimes against humanity.

4
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.650
Human Rights Watch uses satellite imagery
to track the destruction of villages

5
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.430
and city blocks.

6
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.330
So when a government
abuses its own people,

7
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.170
who has the right to step in?

8
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.430
Nobody at all?

9
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.430
Only the UN Security Council?

10
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.910
And how?

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.570
In this mission, you'll
line up interventions,

12
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.830
from development aid to
direct military action.

13
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.910
Then you'll meet the players:
international bodies,

14
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:43.030
governments, and groups
like Amnesty International.

15
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.070
Your mission: decide who has
the right to step in, and how.
